  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">To address the imperative of occupational health, safety (OSH) and hygiene in workplaces, especially in light of the COVID-19 pandemic, the Employers&#x2019; Federation of Ceylon (EFC) introduced a new training module in its annual training calendar. This initiative led to the launch of a new certificate training programme on OSH and hygiene, spanning three training programmes. The most recent instance of this programme, the third consecutive one, took place in May 2023. The demand for such training extended beyond EFC&#x2019;s membership, promoting collaboration with the Free Trade Zone Manufacturing Association in Biyagama and Seethawaka&#x2019;s free trade zones in both 2022 and 2023. Consequently, 106 participants from 79 enterprises across diverse sectors such as garments, tire manufacturing, resin products, tobacco, tea export and glassware manufacturing acquired knowledge and competencies to upgrade workplace OSH and hygiene. They were certified as enterprise health and hygiene ambassadors.  The Health and Hygiene programme&#x2019;s sustainability is ensured through the integration into the 2022 -23 training calendar of the EFC, informed by market research and needs assessment. 
During 2022 -23, EFC undertook enhancements in its training delivery platform and methodology, expanding its training outreach. Initially resorting to online training via video conferencing software during the pandemic, EFC quickly recognized its limitations. As a result, EFC swiftly set up an E-learning platform offering diverse courses in various formats. The E-learning platform enables EFC to enrich its training services in terms of scope, quality, and delivery mechanisms. This expansion not only responds to the immediate needs of members, but aimed at strengthening the efficacy, user-friendliness, and resilience of its training function. EFC has already leveraged this platform, successfully delivering the Executive Diploma in Employment Relations as well as the programme on OSH and hygiene. Building on the interest shown by South Asian employers to promote Health and Hygiene, the ILO designed a Training of Trainers (ToT) programme aimed at enhancing the knowledge and capacities of South Asian employers&#x2019; organizations in OSH and hygiene matters. This programme, conducted online in June 2021, catered to seven South Asian employers&#x2019; organizations. Notably, 23 participants underwent training to become Health and Hygiene Ambassadors of which two came from EFC. The ILO assisted in translating the training modules to Sinhala, enabling EFC Ambassadors to roll out the training within EFC membership and in the Free trade zones.
In supporting EFC, ITC-ILC played a crucial role in setting up the E-learning platform. ITC-ILO trained four EFC officials, including the head of training who serves as the focal point in the management and administration of the platform. This training was facilitated through a 7-week online E-training programme in 2022.</narrative>
   </description>
